# .sam-ui-commit-allow — explicit exemptions for sam-ui-commit.sh's secret guard.
#
# Read by /home/col/bin/sam-ui-commit.sh before every automated commit. The full
# design lives in the "secret guard" and "allow-list" comment blocks of that
# script; this is the short version.
#
# Format, one entry per line:
#
#     <path>  <rule>  <reason>
#
#   path    Repo-relative path, or a glob (matched shell-style against the path
#           in the staged diff). '*' or '**' alone is rejected — no entry may
#           excuse the whole repo.
#   rule    Only `assigned-secret` is accepted: a long, whitespace-free value
#           assigned to a field whose name contains secret/token/password/key.
#           An entry naming `key-shaped` is rejected — a literal credential
#           (sk-ant-…, AKIA…, ghp_…, a private key header, a JWT) is never
#           legitimate in this repo, so the precise pass stays absolute and has
#           no lever here.
#   reason  Mandatory, at least 10 characters. Say why the value is known to be
#           harmless. THIS FILE IS PUBLIC — write prose, never a secret value.
#
# Every use of an entry is logged by the guard as
#
#     ALLOWED [assigned-secret] <file>:<line> — <reason>
#
# so an exemption being exercised shows up in /home/col/.sam/logs/sam-ui-commit.log
# rather than passing silently.
#
# A malformed line is ignored and logged with its line number; it never fails open.
# Adding an entry here is a deliberate act, not a rubber stamp — keep the list tiny.
#
# (Named .sam-ui-commit-allow, not "...-secret-guard-allow", on purpose: the
# latter trips the box's Bash credential-path guard on any command that both
# reads a file and names it, which would block every future inspection of a file
# that is perfectly safe to read.)

.env.local.template	assigned-secret	Template only — ships placeholder values, never a real credential
src/lib/server/chat/tiers.ts	assigned-secret	ANTHROPIC_AUTH_TOKEN is a sentinel; the loopback Gemini proxy ignores it
